WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.771 --> 00:00:21.373
barely eaten all week, Ben," Winnie said.

2
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:25.475
The following week Ben was sitting with his friends in the cafeteria.

3
00:00:26.416 --> 00:00:28.737
His sandwich sat untouched on his tray.

4
00:00:28.757 --> 00:00:32.280
"I'm too worried," Ben said.

5
00:00:33.548 --> 00:00:36.611
"Because of that dumb sinkhole, we've lost almost a whole week.

6
00:00:37.792 --> 00:00:39.853
The garden will never be ready in time for the wedding.

7
00:00:40.414 --> 00:00:42.535
I feel like I'm letting down Victoria and Uncle Bert."

8
00:00:42.555 --> 00:00:45.478
"There's Mr.

9
00:00:45.518 --> 00:00:46.859
Bog," Waldo said.

10
00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:48.880
"Let's ask him about the sinkhole."

11
00:00:50.141 --> 00:00:51.843
He waved to the school custodian.

12
00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:55.005
"Is the sinkhole fixed yet?"

13
00:00:55.025 --> 00:00:58.848
"I just finished filling it," Mr.

14
00:00:58.908 --> 00:00:59.709
Bog replied.

15
00:00:59.729 --> 00:01:03.252
"You can get back to work after school today."

16
00:01:04.284 --> 00:01:05.165
Ben brightened.

17
00:01:05.185 --> 00:01:07.667
"That's the best news I've heard all week!"

18
00:01:08.807 --> 00:01:10.348
"Did you figure out what happened?"

19
00:01:10.629 --> 00:01:11.469
Gaby asked.

20
00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.411
Mr. Bog shrugged.

21
00:01:13.431 --> 00:01:17.433
"Some critter was probably burrowing underground."

22
00:01:17.454 --> 00:01:20.436
"Sounds like we're back in business!"

23
00:01:20.796 --> 00:01:21.817
Ben said happily.

24
00:01:21.837 --> 00:01:24.058
"Let's meet outside right after school!"

25
00:01:27.981 --> 00:01:31.944
When the last bell of the day rang, Ben floated outside to meet his mom.

26
00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:35.325
She was dropping off Sid so he could help with the garden.

27
00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:38.307
"Sorry we're late!"

28
00:01:38.787 --> 00:01:40.488
Mom floated toward him with Sid.

29
00:01:40.508 --> 00:01:44.770
"I saw your text about the sinkhole repair—that's great news."

30
00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:46.310
Ben nodded.

31
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.772
"At least someone has great news," Mom continued.

32
00:01:50.792 --> 00:01:55.214
"Claudia Croaker, who was going to sing at the wedding, got laryngitis.

33
00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.496
How am I going to find another famous opera singer now?

34
00:02:00.224 --> 00:02:01.285
Oh, there's my phone."

35
00:02:01.525 --> 00:02:03.285
Mom pulled her phone out of her purse.

36
00:02:03.305 --> 00:02:05.286
"I'll see you two at home later!"

37
00:02:10.448 --> 00:02:13.910
Ben was pleasantly surprised when he and Sid got to the garden.

38
00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:16.291
Things didn't look too bad.

39
00:02:22.093 --> 00:02:22.993
how pretty!"

40
00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.715
Jen pointed to the field of black-and-orange flowers.

41
00:02:26.735 --> 00:02:29.116
"All the flowers are blooming now."

42
00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:31.280
"And Mr.

43
00:02:31.341 --> 00:02:34.542
Bog dug a new piranha pond for us," Mog said.

44
00:02:34.562 --> 00:02:36.263
"We'll fill it up now.

45
00:02:36.864 --> 00:02:38.685
My mom will be so happy.

46
00:02:39.385 --> 00:02:42.627
She's sick of the piranhas swimming around our bathtub at home."

47
00:02:45.308 --> 00:02:49.871
A few minutes later, Ben headed toward the archway to help Sid and the zombies.

48
00:02:50.651 --> 00:02:53.312
On his way he noticed the ground creeper vines.

49
00:02:53.893 --> 00:02:55.574
They still hadn't grown at all.

50
00:02:55.594 --> 00:02:59.496
"They probably need more fertilizer," Ben mumbled.

51
00:03:02.484 --> 00:03:07.067
He found the bottle sitting near the wheelbarrow and sprinkled some liquid on the vines.

52
00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:13.690
Ben," Gaby called.

53
00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.551
"Can I talk to you for a minute?"

54
00:03:16.572 --> 00:03:20.474
Ben tossed the bottle of fertilizer on the ground and floated over to Gaby.

55
00:03:20.494 --> 00:03:22.095
"Is something wrong?"

56
00:03:22.115 --> 00:03:24.776
"Everything's fine," Gaby said.

57
00:03:24.796 --> 00:03:28.979
"I just wanted to tell you that I have an idea to help Sid with his scaring.

58
00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:31.060
Can I work with him for a little while?"

59
00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:33.217
"Sure," Ben said.

60
00:03:33.237 --> 00:03:39.300
"I could teach him to make himself look big and—" "Yoo-hoo, monsters!"

61
00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:44.763
Mr. Icky was coming toward the Green Club members, pushing a cart full of food and drinks.

62
00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:50.426
"I thought I'd bring you hard-working gardeners some refreshments."

63
00:03:50.446 --> 00:03:56.589
"Mmm." Mog licked his lips, eyeing the cart.

64
00:03:56.609 --> 00:03:59.731
"That food looks great!"

65
00:03:59.811 --> 00:04:01.492
Mr. Icky smiled proudly.

66
00:04:02.184 --> 00:04:05.546
"These are some of the dishes I created to serve at the wedding.

67
00:04:06.486 --> 00:04:09.468
I was hoping you monsters would be my taste testers."

68
00:04:10.169 --> 00:04:11.809
The vampire showed her fangs.

69
00:04:11.829 --> 00:04:14.531
"I'd be happy to take a bite!"

70
00:04:14.551 --> 00:04:19.033
"Everything looks delicious," Ben said.

71
00:04:19.053 --> 00:04:22.755
"I've planned the menu very carefully," Mr.

72
00:04:22.896 --> 00:04:23.516
Icky said.

73
00:04:24.044 --> 00:04:28.607
"We have mini spiderweb soufflés, inspired by your Uncle Bert's recipe.

74
00:04:28.967 --> 00:04:34.311
There are lizard eggs on toast with ant egg dressing, and moldy bacon-wrapped slugs.

75
00:04:35.092 --> 00:04:40.235
For drinks, I've made tarantula cola and sparkling venom-ade."

76
00:04:41.736 --> 00:04:46.199
After the Green Club members had filled their plates, they sat down on the grass to eat the

77
00:04:46.239 --> 00:04:47.240
delicious food.

78
00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:54.316
Even the zombies were wide awake for once, mumbling, "Yum," between bites.

79
00:04:55.637 --> 00:04:58.998
Ben put his plate down on the grass while he drank his venom-ade.

80
00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:03.200
But when he reached for the plate again, it was empty.

81
00:05:05.721 --> 00:05:06.662
"Hey!" he said.

82
00:05:06.682 --> 00:05:08.242
"Who took my food?"

83
00:05:09.103 --> 00:05:10.843
Then Jen frowned at her plate.

84
00:05:11.684 --> 00:05:14.325
"Somebody took my slugs!"

85
00:05:14.345 --> 00:05:17.126
"And somebody finished my drink!"

86
00:05:17.606 --> 00:05:18.787
a fish monster cried.

87
00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.908
Ben looked around for his little brother.

88
00:05:22.284 --> 00:05:22.945
"Where's Sid?"

89
00:05:23.165 --> 00:05:23.665
he muttered.

90
00:05:23.685 --> 00:05:25.727
"Did he make himself invisible again?"

91
00:05:25.747 --> 00:05:27.989
"I'm right here!"

92
00:05:28.289 --> 00:05:30.311
Sid replied from his spot next to Gaby.

93
00:05:30.331 --> 00:05:34.174
"He's been sitting with me the whole time," Gaby added.

94
00:05:34.194 --> 00:05:36.396
"We've been—" "Help!"

95
00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:37.957
Mr. Icky cried.

96
00:05:37.977 --> 00:05:39.478
"My cart!"

97
00:05:40.079 --> 00:05:45.223
The monsters looked over at the cooking teacher, who was racing after his cart as it rolled away.

98
00:05:45.243 --> 00:05:47.165
"I can't catch it!"

99
00:05:47.225 --> 00:05:48.125
Mr. Icky cried.

100
00:05:49.306 --> 00:05:50.908
Mog jumped up to grab the cart.

101
00:05:52.736 --> 00:05:57.580
He was able to yank it back, but then his foot slipped, and the cart shot forward again.

102
00:05:58.261 --> 00:06:02.705
For a few minutes, it zigzagged all over, sending everyone scattering.

103
00:06:03.425 --> 00:06:07.509
Finally it tipped over, spilling dishes and food onto the ground.

104
00:06:07.529 --> 00:06:12.693
"Ugh." Ben floated up to survey the scene.

105
00:06:12.713 --> 00:06:19.779
"If I weren't a ghost," he thought, "I'd be convinced this garden was haunted!"
